{
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"93a7921e2b686d87",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Stimulus**\nWater potential of Blood increases eg: due to large intake of water",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-540,
			"y":180,
			"width":250,
			"height":160,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"a080bf304f8f0d58",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Receptor**\nHypothalamus is stimulated",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":-60,
			"width":250,
			"height":100,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"6b74aea55f969ee6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Corrective Mechanism**\n* less ADH produced by hypothalamus + released by pituitary gland into the bloodstream\n* less ADH transported to the kidneys\n* Cells in the walls of the collecting ducts and distal convoluted tubule become less permeable to water\n* Less water selectively reabsorbed into the bloodstream BY OSMOSIS\n* More water excreted\n* Urine is more diluted\n* More urine is produced\nClosely linked to: [[How is Urine Formed]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-140,
			"y":-560,
			"width":520,
			"height":480,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"c2f5fe38b2dff7d9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-415,
			"y":80,
			"width":50,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"a4956bc0bd7c79cc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Normal Water potential in Blood",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-270,
			"y":480,
			"width":320,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"bcebe2409cd8fd79",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Stimulus**\nWater potential of blood decreases eg: due to loss of water through profuse sweating",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-703,
			"y":774,
			"width":250,
			"height":206
		},
		{
			"id":"1baa8055198414fc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Corrective Mechanism**\n* more ADH produced by hypothalamus +  released by pituitary gland into the bloodstream. \n* more ADH transported to the kidneys.\n* Cells in the walls of the collecting ducts and distal convoluted tubule become more permeable to water\n* more water selectively reabsorbed into bloodstream BY OSMOSIS. \n* Urine is more concentrated\n* less urine produced. \n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-235,
			"y":1360,
			"width":455,
			"height":420
		},
		{
			"id":"78abb7d6256c6f90",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Receptor**\n=> hypothalamus is stimulated",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-703,
			"y":1200,
			"width":250,
			"height":99
		},
		{
			"id":"7d56ffa94d48b009",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Water Potential of blood increases to the normal level.\nSends feedback to receptor (hypothalamus) -> to reduce ADH production -> less is secreted by pituitary gland. \n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":240,
			"y":920,
			"width":320,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"7fe220ec45f33ada",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-390,
			"y":640,
			"width":50,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"ac3c2a552bc81016",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-603,
			"y":1002,
			"width":50,
			"height":58
		},
		{
			"id":"0b31c29a79bc4f4c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Water Potential of Blood decreases to the normal level\nSends *feedback* to the receptor (hypothalamus) -> to increase ADH production -> more is released by pituitary gland.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":420,
			"y":50,
			"width":340,
			"height":210,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"ad08ef8c371345e9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-330,
			"y":390,
			"width":70,
			"height":60
		},
