		},
		{
			"id":"0cbc45a94e64fced",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"5",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":80,
			"y":690,
			"width":80,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"d401cd2c00ca4c62",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Refer to chapter 8 [[Excretion in Humans Main Note]]\n=> ADH acts on kidneys to help regulate WP of blood in the body through osmoregulation. \n=> ADH affects reabsorption of water in the kidneys.\nLess ADH results in more urine production and more ADH results in less urine production.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-835,
			"y":-800,
			"width":460,
			"height":280
		},
		{"id":"30939603997dc31b","type":"text","text":"Note: \n- ADH -> produced in hypothalamus \n- secreted by pituitary gland\n","x":-1000,"y":-400,"width":320,"height":166,"color":"4"}
	],
